nn5le09ob01re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Asking If or When People are Free", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "When you want to spend time with someone, you ask them if or when they are free.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You use these phrases to ask people if or when they are free:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I am/was wondering if ...<br /> Are you free on/in ... ?<br /> How does (day) sound?<br /> When are you free to ... ?<br /> What day are you free on?", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I was wondering if you wanted to go to the park. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Are you free in the morning? ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "How does Sunday sound? ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "When are you free to get some ice cream? <br/> <br/> <br/>", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " The First Conditional", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " You can use the first conditional to talk about actions and situations in the future.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "There are two parts to the sentence. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "One part is the <span class =\"strong\">condition</span>. The other part is the <span class =\"strong\">result</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Form:<br /><span class=\"italic\"> If + subject + Simple Present tense  + subject + will</span><br />  You use a comma after the condition in this form. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You can flip the two parts of the sentence so that the result comes first.  It can be in interrogative form. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Form:<br /><span class=\"italic\"> Will + subject + if + subject + Simple Present tense ?</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class =\\\"strong\\\"> Condition </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class =\\\"strong\\\">Result</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> If we don't go, </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> I will send you a text. </span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "&nbsp;", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class =\\\"strong\\\"> Result </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class =\\\"strong\\\"> Condition </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> Will you text me  </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> when you arrive at the park? </span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "weather forecast", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a description of what kind of weather is likely to happen in the future ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The weather forecast for tomorrow looks great.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le09ob01aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you use to talk about activities you can do outside.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "playground", "type": "name"}, {"content": "an area that often has special equipment for kids to play on ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We can visit the playground in the park.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le09ob01aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to feed", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to give food to ", "type": "definition"},